What *exactly* did you upgrade? BTW upgrades from distributors in linux
are problematic at best. You have no way of knowing if the developers
got all the configuration changes right and compiled the same. They
often don't. 


It looks to me like you have problems with libc. You can be sure by
changing to /usr/include and grepping all files for tgetstr. Midnight
Commander does this from it's command menu (run mc or gmc to get it- F1
for help). Also Try /usr/local/include as well. This will give you the
include file that references the library. If it *is* found, then you
have linking problems and the command line for the link doesn't include
those directorys. If not, then you are missing libraries. Were you
trying to compile the gui version? Do you have the QT development
library installed? You need it if so. 

